.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH geectl-gitea-raw-file 1  "geectl-gitea-raw-file 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-gitea\-raw\-file \- Print one file from a repository verbatim. Content command: the text IS the file content, with no header. `\-\-ref` reads from a branch, tag, or commit instead of the default branch. A missing file is `NotFound`, never empty content — the 404 is the existence answer
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl gitea raw\-file\fR [\fB\-\-ref\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIOWNER\fR> <\fIREPO\fR> <\fIPATH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print one file from a repository verbatim. Content command: the text IS the file content, with no header. `\-\-ref` reads from a branch, tag, or commit instead of the default branch. A missing file is `NotFound`, never empty content — the 404 is the existence answer
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-ref\fR \fI<GIT_REF>\fR
The branch, tag, or commit to read from; the default branch when omitted
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIOWNER\fR>
The repository owner
.TP
<\fIREPO\fR>
The repository name
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
The file path inside the repository
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
